 "bloques": [
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Greeting and saying goodbye",
   "texto": [
    "**안녕하세요** is good to say hello to anyone at any time.",
    "To say goodbye, there are two sentences, according to who's leaving. Al que **se marcha** le dices **안녕히 가세요** («vaya en paz»). **se queda**, **안녕히 계세요** («Be at peace.»).",
    "When you meet someone: **만나서 반갑습니다** (happy to meet you), or shorter, **반갑습니다**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "I am",
   "texto": [
    "«To be» is attached behind the name: **이에요** if the word ends in consonant and **예요** if it ends in vocal.",
    "학생 → **학생이에요** (soy estudiante). 의사 → **의사예요** (soy médico).",
    "To ask, it doesn't change anything: just raise your voice in the end. **학생이에요?** = are you a student?"
   ]
